{
	"_readme": [
		"The whole quest, walked: the warden, a gate that refuses, the key in the hollow, the gate",
		"opening on the KEY ITSELF rather than on a flag, a lantern that refuses because it is dry,",
		"the hermit's oil two maps away, and the lantern lit with it.",
		"",
		"It is the only gate that proves items end to end - that a chest hands one over, that a door",
		"reads what is carried, that a lock refuses without it and says why, and that a consumable",
		"is actually consumed. Every unit test above it works on a snapshot; this one works on the",
		"player's own bag.",
		"",
		"Every leg is held until a WALL or a BODY stops it, so nothing here counts tiles: the one",
		"exception is the slide down the village's east wall, where the number of frames only has to",
		"be enough to reach the gate's row - past it is fine, because the gate fires on arrival.",
		"",
		"The routes look roundabout because they are: an arriving hold carries the player onward into",
		"the next map, so most legs begin by re-anchoring against a wall rather than assuming where",
		"the previous one left off."
	],
